$draw_text — overlay multiline text on input images

SUMMARY
  Draws white text with black outline on each image in images[] using Pillow.

SYNTAX
  $draw_text
  $draw_text(text='Hello^World')
  $draw_text(font='ttf/MuseoSansCyrl-700.ttf', size=40, left=30, top=350)

INPUT
  images[] — source images (required)
  prompts[] or texts[] — text to draw; one entry per image, or one for all

OUTPUT
  images[] — new image links with text rendered (replaces input image links)

ARGUMENTS
  text=         — fixed text for every image (overrides prompts[]/texts[])
  font=         — path to .ttf file (default: ttf/MuseoSansCyrl-700.ttf under repo root)
  size=         — font size in pixels (default: 40)
  left= / top=  — text position (default: 30, 350); clamped to stay inside image
  spacing=      — line spacing (default: 6)
  stroke_width= — outline width (default: 2)

TEXT RULES
  If len(text) > 10, caret ^ in text is replaced with newline.

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_DRAW_TEXT=1 — copy source bytes with marker, no Pillow.

DEPENDENCIES
  uv sync --extra draw_text   (Pillow)

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No — prompts[] and texts[] pass through unless used as text source.

EXAMPLE
  @caption
  Line one^Line two

  @overlay: @images -> @caption -> $draw_text
